From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mcla-x86 SDK patch layer
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 0440: guest vblank locked to the display's real vblank (phase and rate), every k-th one

Source: Ours, written for this SDK (ORC fix after the W3.4 M4 gate failure; the display-lock design of the ORC task).
  The idea of following the display's vblank is $IOS's display-locked guest vblank (docs/mcla/TIMING.md, ios_vblank_*);
  nothing is copied (that one is CADisplayLink)
Licence: GPL-3 (owner's own work, part of mcla-x86); the patched files are ReXGlue SDK code (BSD-3-Clause)
Purpose: With guest_vblank_precise and guest_vblank_display_lock (GPU, bool, default true) the guest's vblank grid takes
  its phase and rate from the real vblank of the display the game window is on, every k-th vblank when the display
  refreshes at k x video_mode_refresh_rate within 0.5 % (120 Hz panel: k = 2). A helper thread waits on
  IDXGIOutput::WaitForVBlank; the vblank thread fits a line to its last 128 vblanks and times the guest's vblank on that
  line with the timer + QPC spin of 0400. Falls back to the QPC grid (src=qpc) when the rate does not fit, the display
  stops, or the output fails. `[guest-vblank] ... n=<count> src=display|qpc`. Cvar guest_vblank_display_offset_us (0).
  Windows only. Not built before the next SDK build.
Bucket: REDO

0440-guest-vblank-display-lock.patch (mcla-x86 ORC fix; evidence in $WORK/scratch/W3.2/present_jitter.md)

Why. Presents in the W3.4 runs are composed by the DWM (PresentMon: "Composed: Flip", SyncInterval 0, flags 0x204, never
blocking) and shown at the panel's vblank, 120.000 Hz (fitted from MsUntilDisplayed). The guest's QPC grid is 2 x 60.000
against it, so it never beats, but its PHASE against the panel is whatever the vblank thread's first QPC reading made
it, a different one every run. The share of frames held more than 40 ms was 8.2 % in the one run with MsUntilDisplayed
p50 20.0 ms and 20-24 % in the runs with p50 10-11 ms, at the same 33.3 ms present cadence and the same present
jitter (sd 0.83-0.86 ms): consistent with the present landing at a different distance from the DWM's composition
deadline in each run (an inference from those two columns; the DWM's deadline is not measured). With the grid locked to
the display, the guest's vblank, hence the swap gate's release and the present, comes at a fixed offset after the
panel's vblank in every run, tunable with guest_vblank_display_offset_us (and on a 59.94 / 119.88 Hz panel the guest
follows the panel instead of beating against it once every ~16 s).

Design. The wake-ups of WaitForVBlank are not good enough to time the guest's vblank on directly: measured on this
machine (a 120 Hz panel, 2,399 waits) they scatter with sd 0.155 ms, p99 0.36 ms, max 0.56 ms around an exact
119.9993 Hz line, and a guest vblank fired on every second wake would inherit that (period sd 0.22 ms). So:
  * Helper thread (DisplayVblankThread, "GPU Display VBlank", time-critical): the DXGI output of the game window's
    monitor, WaitForVBlank in a loop, publishes the QPC time of each wake in a ring (count + 256 stamps). WaitForVBlank
    has no time-out, so it is not on the vblank thread: a display that turns off must not stop the guest's vblank.
  * The game window is the largest visible top-level window of the process, looked up every 2 s (MonitorFromWindow); the
    helper is restarted when the window changes monitor. If no output is found or WaitForVBlank fails: warning, retry in 5 s.
  * Vblank thread (PreciseVblank::UpdateDisplayLock, once per vblank): takes the new stamps, keeps a least-squares line
    time(j) = fit_t + (j - fit_j) x fit_period through the last 128 (a stamp more than 2 ms off the line is a late
    wake-up and is dropped; nine in a row restart the line), usable from 48 stamps with rms scatter under 1 ms.
  * Lock: k = round(guest period / fitted display period) with 1 <= k <= 16 and |k x display period - guest period| <=
    0.5 % of the guest period. Then the guest's vblank number n is the display vblank lock_tick + n k, timed with the same
    waitable timer + QPC spin as the QPC grid (so it keeps the grid's precision: the line's noise is the stamps' noise
    / sqrt(128)), plus guest_vblank_display_offset_us. The guest's period is k x the display's, so it follows a
    59.94 Hz panel. A vblank more than one period late fires at once and re-seats lock_tick (resync, no burst).
  * Unlock (-> the QPC grid, anchored at the last vblank, `display lock off (reason)` logged): no stamp for 4 display
    periods + 50 ms (at once), the rate not fitting for 30 vblanks in a row, the cvar off, the helper failing.
  * The stats line gains ` src=display|qpc` after n=.
  * src/graphics/CMakeLists.txt: rexgpu-xenos links dxgi on Windows (it already does with D3D12; a Vulkan-only build
    needs it now).
Harness (the class compiled standalone, a small visible window on this machine's 120 Hz panel, an independent
WaitForVBlank observer, 60 Hz guest, display lock on): guest period mean 16.6669 sd 0.0113 ms (p99 16.685, max 16.901 right
after the lock) against sd 0.0014 for the QPC grid; guest vblank minus the nearest display vblank: mean +0.012 sd
0.164 ms (the observer's own wake-up noise; the QPC grid sits at a fixed but arbitrary phase, -0.94 ms in that run, and
differs run to run). 30 Hz guest: k = 4, sd 0.156; 120 Hz guest: k = 1, sd 0.153; 144 Hz guest: no integer multiple,
`display lock not used`, src=qpc; offset 2000 us: +2.019 ms; a 60 ms stall of the guest: resync 1, lock kept.

Not built or run in the game (clang++ 20.1.8 -fsyntax-only with the SDK's Release flags: no new diagnostics).
Verify: `display lock on: output 120.0xx Hz ... every 2 of them` then `... src=display` in the 10 s lines, p50 16.666-16.667,
p99 <= 16.9; PresentMon MsBetweenDisplayChange share > 40 ms the same in every run (and low); A/B
--guest_vblank_display_lock=false (src=qpc).

